#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
VELVET · velvet-ai

Velly's brain stem. The island's long press starts this program; it reads a
request file, talks to a model, runs the tools the model asks for, and streams
everything it does into ~/.config/velvet/ai-state.json — in place, because the
shell watches that exact inode.

Three things are deliberate here:

  · **The session gate.** Every tool execution re-reads
    ~/.config/velvet/ai-session.json and refuses when the shell is not
    holding a session open. Velly has access to everything, but only while
    you are the one who opened her: the file is written by the shell when the
    long press lands and closed when the island goes away. A sidecar that
    outlives its session can still talk, but it cannot touch anything.

  · **Honesty over magic.** No key and no local model is a normal state, not
    an error to hide: the state file says `brain: none`, the shell shows
    NO BRAIN, and a small local skill set (time, volume, apps, tasks, lock …)
    keeps the important half working without any provider at all.

  · **Streaming to a file.** Tokens are written to ai-state.json as they arrive
    (throttled), so the island can type them out while the model is still
    talking. Nothing here knows what the shell looks like.

Stdlib only, like everything in bin/.

    velvet-ai --selftest          offline checks, no network, no shell
    velvet-ai --ask "wie spät"    one turn, print the answer
    velvet-ai --daemon            the mode the shell starts
    velvet-ai --stt file.wav      transcribe (needs a provider that has ears)
    velvet-ai --learn             distil the last session into memory
    velvet-ai --config            what is configured, without the secret
    velvet-ai --tools             the tool catalogue
    velvet-ai --probe             one round trip to the provider, honestly reported
    velvet-ai --forget-all        wipe the remembered facts and notes
    velvet-ai --tidy-memory       drop junk and duplicate facts (runs after every learn)
"""

import base64
import glob
import difflib
import inspect
import json
